@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:architecture] llm-layer-provider-agnostic
Code under `lib/api/llm` must not encode a specific lab, host, region or model's wire format: no
parsing or construction of a provider's request, response or error bodies, no import from a
provider SDK, no match on a provider's message strings. Recognizing and extracting those specifics
belongs to the provider's own code under `lib/model_constructors/sdk/<sdk>/`,
`lib/model_constructors/providers/<lab>/` or `lib/model_constructors/stream/clients/`, which must
hand the result to this layer through a lab-agnostic field on `ErrorContent` or
`EndpointMetadata.content`.
Reading `lab`, `host`, `region` or `model` to route a request, select credentials, gate a capability
or render a display name remains allowed.
